[h1]Military Drop - Radio Supply Airdrops[/h1]

[b]Build 42.21 · Singleplayer & Multiplayer · Work in progress[/b]

Tune a military radio to the right frequency, give the authentication code, and request an airdrop of military surplus. A helicopter flies in and drops a supply crate... and the noise draws the dead.

[h2]Planned features[/h2]

[list]
[*]Call a supply drop with a military walkie-talkie or HAM radio.
[*]The frequency is found on notes carried by military and police zombies. The authentication code changes every in-game week: a numbers station sends it encrypted, and military codebooks decipher it (or, in the sandbox options, a fixed or weekly code written in clear on the notes).
[*]A helicopter you can hear and see approach: moving sound, rotor shadow on the ground, direction marker.
[*]Crate loot comes from the game's army distribution tables, so it works with weapon mods.
[*]Anyone listening on the frequency hears the drop coordinates, and the spot is marked on their map.
[*]Earn the base's trust as a faction: daily reports, soldiers' dog tags, public missions and a command post radio.
[*]Server-authoritative multiplayer, with one server-wide cooldown set in the sandbox options.
[*]Standalone: no other mod required. Compatible with HEF - Helicopter Event Framework. With Signal Smoke, green smoke marks the crate.
[/list]

[h2]Credits[/h2]

Build 42 rewrite of [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3259615085]Expanded Helicopter Events: Drop Military Cargo[/url] (Build 41). Source code (MIT) on [url=https://github.com/cyberbobjr/BATMAN_EHE_MILITARY_DROP]GitHub[/url].
